    <button type="button" class="faith-glossary-letter" data-faith-glossary-letter="z">Z</button>
  </nav>

  <p class="faith-search-status" data-faith-glossary-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

  {{!-- Letter browse: a flat list of term buttons, 50 at a time. --}}
  <div class="faith-glossary-terms" data-faith-glossary-terms hidden></div>
  <button type="button" class="faith-glossary-more" data-faith-glossary-more hidden>Show more</button>

  {{!-- Search results / an opened term: full definitions. --}}
  <ol class="faith-glossary-entries" data-faith-glossary-entries></ol>

  <div class="faith-glossary-empty" data-faith-glossary-empty hidden>
    <p>No terms found. Try a shorter word, or browse by letter above.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="faith-glossary-note">
    Definitions are drawn from the works that use each term and attributed to the author and page they came from. Where a work's own English gloss wasn't available, the definition was extracted by AI from the surrounding text &mdash; see <a href="/the-faith-received/transparency/">Translation Transparency</a> for how the library discloses AI-assisted text generally. These have not been reviewed by a human editor.
  </p>
</div>
